course: dictionary
lesson: 11707
title: Words about hearing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Auditory is an adjective, so it describes a noun. It means about hearing or the ears. To remember it, think of audio, which is sound you can hear.
explain: «The doctor checked the auditory nerve.» Here auditory tells you the nerve is part of hearing. Nerves work like wires that carry messages around the body.
explain: «Our science class drew the auditory system.» The auditory system is the ears and the parts of the body that help us hear. Auditory often appears in science lessons about the body.
fact: Auditory means about hearing or the ears.
fact: «Auditory» is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as an auditory nerve.
fact: The auditory nerve carries sound signals from the ear to the brain.
fact: You may meet the phrases «auditory nerve» and «auditory system».
fact: Some people call themselves «auditory learners», but the idea that everyone has one fixed learning style is a myth. People learn well in many ways.
exercise: «The doctor tested the child's auditory nerve.» What does auditory mean here? | *About hearing or the ears | About tasting food | About seeing or the eyes | About moving the legs
exercise: Which word means about hearing? | Visual | *Auditory | Olfactory | Tactile
exercise: «The auditory nerve sends messages from the ear.» Where do those messages go? | To the eyes | To the stomach | To the feet | *To the brain
test: «Her auditory system works well, so she heard the bell at once.» What does auditory describe? | *The sense of hearing | The sense of smell | The sense of taste | The sense of touch
test: «Some people say they are auditory learners, but learning styles are a myth.» What does the text say about learning styles? | They are only for adults | They are the same as the auditory nerve | They are proven facts | *They are a myth
exam: Which is the best meaning of auditory? | Able to see in the dark | Quick and strong | *About hearing or the ears | About the sense of smell
